    "section": "Why skew hurts performance",
    "timestamp": "12:14",
    "updatedAt": "2026-08-13T11:12:00.000Z",
    "content": "A skewed tree behaves more like a linked list because each operation follows a long single path. That is why balance is not cosmetic; it directly affects runtime."
  },
  {
