    "topic": "Breadth-first search",
    "sourceType": "notes",
    "sourceName": "Google Drive Lecture 09 Notes",
    "section": "BFS intuition",
    "page": 3,
    "updatedAt": "2026-08-13T10:15:00.000Z",
    "content": "Breadth-first search explores a graph level by level. A queue preserves the frontier, ensuring nodes discovered earlier are expanded first. BFS is useful for shortest path reasoning in unweighted graphs."
  },
