    "section": "Queue operations",
    "page": 8,
    "updatedAt": "2026-08-13T10:18:00.000Z",
    "content": "The BFS queue enqueues neighbors when they are first discovered. Marking visited nodes early prevents duplicate expansion and keeps the traversal bounded."
